# java.android.security.exported_activity.exported_activity: MainActivity is
# the app's launcher activity (MAIN/LAUNCHER intent-filter) — Android
# requires android:exported="true" on any activity with an intent-filter
# since API 31; the manifest merger fails the build without it. Inline
# `nosemgrep` comments (tried both as a preceding line and a same-line
# trailing comment) were not honoured by Semgrep's XML/Android-manifest
# scanner for this rule, so this path-level entry is used instead.
#
# Be aware this is broader than a single-finding suppression: unlike the
# fingerprint-scoped .gitleaksignore entries elsewhere in this repo, a
# .semgrepignore path entry excludes the WHOLE file from ALL Semgrep rules,
# not just this one rule/line — Semgrep has no per-rule, per-line ignore
# mechanism for XML analyzers that this repo's tooling can rely on. This
# file is currently small and single-purpose (manifest declarations only,
# one activity, one provider), so the practical risk is low, but if this
# file grows to include more components in future, review it manually
# before assuming new content here is still covered by this note — this
# entry does not know the difference between old and new content.
